    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b99ef638-3334-5ac6-8589-7c9e3d58c6cd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =0\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "58750e11-86aa-5ab0-9f8a-b5d69ee8751f",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
